Fixes https://github.com/MarinhoFeliphe/liferay-portal/issues/358

This PR aim to provide a better UX using context modal.

- contextModal's functions now correctly infer modalKeys, providing autocompletion and strong typescript support.
```ts
openContextModal({ modalKey: 'myCustomModal' });
updateContextModal({ modalKey: 'myCustomModal' });
closeContextModal('myCustomModal');
```

- Fix closeContextModal to correctly work with modalKey

- Make innerProps optionnal when not needed
```ts
// Without InnerProps
openContextModal({ modalKey: 'customWithNoInner' });
updateContextModal({ modalKey: 'customWithNoInner' });

// With InnerProps
openContextModal({ innerProps: { text: 'example' }, modalKey: 'customWithInner' });
updateContextModal({ innerProps: { text: 'example' }, modalKey: 'customWithInner' });
```

- Strong typing for `ModalsProvider`
```tsx
const signInModals = { signInStepOne: SignInStepOneModal, signInStepTwo: SignInStepTwoModal };
export type SignInModals = typeof signInModals;

const registerModals = { registerStepOne: RegisterStepOneModal, registerStepTwo: RegisterStepTwoModal };
export type RegisterModals = typeof registerModals;

declare module '@mantine/modals' {
  export interface MantineModalsOverride {
    modals: SignInModals & RegisterModals;
  }
}

<ModalsProvider modals={{ ...signInModals }}> /* Typescript error, missing registerModals */
```

- 1:1 parity between function from `useModals` hook and events exported by `@mantine/modals` to avoid confusion
```ts
// Before
openContextModal('myCustomModal', { innerProps: { text: '' } }); // Hook
openContextModal({ modal: 'myCustomModal', innerProps: { text: '' } }); // Event

closeContextModal(); // Only by hook, no re-exported event

closeAll(); // Hook
closeAllModals(); // Event

// After
openContextModal({ modalKey: 'myCustomModal', innerProps: { text: '' } }); // Hook & Event
closeContextModal('myCustomModal'); // Hook & Event
closeAllModals(); // Hook & Event
```

contextModal's function will use `modalKey` to properly differentiate with `modalId`. Before, `openContextModal` required a prop named `modal` or `modalId` depending on how it was used (hook vs event). Also, contextModals can still use the proper `modalId` prop along `modalKey`, so that differentiation make sense to me.

This PR include some breaking change:

1. `closeContextModal` now works with `modalKey`, previsouly it was just a duplicate of `closeModal` and only worked with `modalId` even tho it was typed to works with `modalKey`.
2. `openContextModal` has a different signature when used with `useModals` or when imported. Now it share a single signature.
3. `closeAllModals` has different names when used with `useModals` or when imported. Now it share a single name.
4. If there's no `innerProps` for a contextModal, `innerProps` will become optional, and this PR typed it as `never` so the old fashion will produce an error. This can be modified to either allow settling a "wrong" innerProps, or keep it like this to avoid unecessary code.
```ts
openContextModal({ modal: 'myCustomModal', innerProps: {} }); // Type '{}' is not assignable to type 'undefined'.
```

I originally only wanted to enforce correct typing and provide autocompletion to contextModal, but then I realize closeContextModal was wrongly typed and the fix could be a breaking change, so I end up proposing all this.

I'll be happy to modify things if needed, and if you accept the following modification, I can also work on some documentation.

Thanks !

Addresses feedback on #28 regarding improper transaction abort handling in `acceptMatchRequest`.

## Problem

The error path was calling `session.endSession()` immediately after `abortTransaction()`, before throwing. This caused the finally block to attempt session cleanup a second time, creating potential failures and race conditions.

```typescript
// Before - problematic
if (!request) {
  await session.abortTransaction();
  session.endSession();  // ← Redundant, finally block also does this
  throw new Error(`Match request with ID ${id} not found`);
}

// After - fixed
if (!request) {
  await session.abortTransaction();
  throw new Error(`Match request with ID ${id} not found`);
}
```

## Changes

- Removed redundant `session.endSession()` call from error path in `acceptMatchRequest`
- Session cleanup now handled exclusively by finally block, ensuring single cleanup regardless of exit path

